<title>SENEGAL: U.S. gives Senegal $16.5 million in health aid.</title>
<headline>U.S. gives Senegal $16.5 million in health aid.</headline>
<dateline>DAKAR 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States has given Senegal $16.5 millions to help fund health and population projects, U.S. officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>A statement said the money would be used to fund projects such as birth control and fighting AIDS in the West African nation. It is part of a 1997 global grant worth $21 million.</p>
